{"chunk_id": "f7e74c121d68", "text": "After hearing the legend of the cosmic fish, Yudhishthira asks the immortal sage Markandeya to explain the deeper causes of creation and destruction, since the sage has witnessed many cosmic cycles. Markandeya begins by praising the supreme being\u2014Janardana (Vishnu)\u2014the eternal source who creates and withdraws the universe. He explains the vast cycles of time: the four Yugas and the immense \u201cday of Brahma.\u201d As the Kali Yuga declines, social order collapses\u2014truth fades, castes abandon their duties, rulers become corrupt, famine spreads, and morality decays. Eventually cosmic destruction arrives: multiple suns dry the earth, a universal fire consumes creation, and immense clouds flood the world for years. Markandeya recounts wandering alone across the cosmic ocean until he sees a mysterious divine child on a banyan tree. Entering the child\u2019s body, he beholds the entire universe within, revealing Vishnu\u2019s infinite cosmic nature and the illusion (maya) of creation.\nMarkandeya describes cosmic cycles, Kali Yuga\u2019s moral decline, the fiery-pralayic destruction of the universe, and his vision of the divine child containing the cosmos within.\nThemes: cosmic cycles and yugas, Kali Yuga degeneration, apocalyptic destruction, divine illusion (maya), vision of Vishnu as cosmic child", "vector": [0.010620263405144215, -0.017030086368322372, 0.010142721235752106, 0.003662275616079569, -0.023688768967986107, -0.0003690861049108207, -0.03492109477519989, -0.015483119525015354, -0.017393287271261215, -0.006258489564061165, 0.019774271175265312, 0.02543751522898674, -0.009369238279759884, 0.030697202309966087, -0.009409593418240547, 0.00587847363203764, 0.04764657840132713, -0.0042104399763047695, 0.029109878465533257, -0.026002494618296623, -0.0015217445325106382, 0.010546278208494186, 0.003985120914876461, -0.00897913333028555, -0.01281964685767889, 0.02800682559609413, 0.022948915138840675, -0.0297017619